    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` requires that a successful owner create emits an `AUDIT` log line containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\nI kept structural impact minimal by adding behaviour as a **new, self-contained function** rather than modifying any existing method:\n\n1. **New class** `LogAuditOnCreate.java` \u2014 one public `service(@Val Owner owner)` method that logs via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`. As a fresh class, `WMC_other = 0` and `CC = 1`, so its cost is just its own line count.\n\n2. **One YAML edit** in `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `logAudit` step between `save` (which assigns the id) and `respond`, keeping the same `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\nNo existing complex function was touched, so the WMC_other lever stays low; only 2 files are in the multiplier. The audit line reads e.g. `owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07`, satisfying the `anyContains` assertion. Full test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
